            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="0696" n="586" xml:id="pg586"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2932: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-27T20:00:00+08:00">November 27 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >28?</hi>], 1931—8 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 28—7:58
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1019. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 27, 1 p.m. Official spokesman gave out following statement from
                            Japanese headquarters but stated that it was to be taken as unofficial:
                                <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <p>‘In view of the fact that the present situation has become
                                    quieter, headquarters has decided to withdraw all troops to the
                                    east of the Liao River and establish them at points within the
                                    South Manchuria Railway zone. The number of troops outside the
                                    zone will be reduced to a minimum.’”</p>
                            </quote></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
